                <a:cs typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202090204" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>How far are proposals from what already exists in the scientific literature? Measured as mean cosine distance from each proposal to its 10 nearest neighbors in a corpus of 350 PubMed articles. Higher = more novel. Crucially different from diversity: a group can be internally diverse but still close to published work, or internally homogeneous but exploring genuinely new territory.</a:t></a:r>
